From 090ce5f56615791faa262fae4f1382ab73f9436c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:01:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usage): keep four metrics on the run usage card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The per-turn card carried six cells. Cache hit rate and cost are dropped:
the hit-rate cell only restated the cache-read number beside it, and the
estimated cost never resolved for relay/custom providers — the pricing table
is keyed by the configured provider id (`custom:octopus`) while the usage
ledger records the bare family name (`custom`), and the panel's provider
picker only offers the configured id, so that cell read `—` on every run.

The card now shows output / input / cache-read / token speed: 2x2 in a narrow
message column, one row of four once the card is wider than 440px. The
summary payload keeps both fields — the usage dashboard still uses them.
